This returns 0 for any (x, z). So v1 doesn't have a heightmap wired up — it's all flat. The pad detection works because the integrator uses `terrainY = planet.radius + heightAt(nextPos.x, nextPos.z)` which is just `planet.radius` for flat terrain.

So for v1, the pad's world position is `planetCenter + (localX, planet.radius, localZ)`. The pad sits on the surface of the planet at local-to-planet-center coords `(localX, localZ)`.

This means I need to update the pads.ts to use `planet.radius` as the pad's height (not the heightmap value, since the heightmap isn't wired up in v1).

